      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-159694",
      ":question/problem": "Let $X = [X_{1}, X_{2}]^{T}$ be a bivariate normal random vector with mean vector $\u03bc$ and covariance matrix $\u03a3$ given by\n$\u03bc = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}, \u03a3 = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nLet $Y = X_{1} - 2X_{2}$. Calculate $P(Y \\ge 1)$.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $\u03a6(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $\u03a6(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution.*\n\n| $z$ | $0.03$ | $0.04$ | $0.05$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $0.8$ | $0.7967$ | $0.7995$ | $0.8023$ |\n| $0.9$ | $0.8238$ | $0.8264$ | $0.8289$ |\n| $1.0$ | $0.8485$ | $0.8508$ | $0.8531$ |\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
